# AP Macroeconomics — master IDs 02-xxx plus research expansion. Pending teacher review.
@subject ap-macroeconomics | AP Macroeconomics | AP 宏观经济学 | Macro | cyan | 5
@desc The economy as a whole: output, inflation, unemployment, money, policy and international trade.
@framework Unit titles follow the AP Macroeconomics course framework (6 units).

@unit 1 | Basic Economic Concepts | 基本经济概念
- scarcity | 稀缺性 | Limited resources relative to unlimited wants | 资源有限而欲望无限，宏观层面同样需要取舍。 | Scarcity forces a nation to choose between military and civilian goods on its PPC. | 1
- production possibilities curve | 生产可能性曲线 | A graph of the maximum output combinations of two goods | 资源和技术给定时两种商品的最大产量组合，向外移动表示经济增长。 | An increase in capital stock shifts the PPC outward. | 2
  vis: ppc
- economic growth | 经济增长 | An increase in an economy's capacity to produce, shown by an outward PPC or rightward LRAS shift | 生产能力的提高，表现为 PPC 外移或 LRAS 右移。 | Investment in education promotes long-run economic growth. | 2

@unit 2 | Economic Indicators and the Business Cycle | 经济指标与经济周期
- gross domestic product | 国内生产总值 | The market value of all final goods and services produced within a country in a period | 一国在一定时期内生产的所有最终商品和服务的市场价值。只算最终产品，避免重复计算。 | A used car sale is not counted in GDP because it was produced in an earlier year. | 1 | #02-001
  mis: GDP includes all sales — it excludes used goods, intermediate goods and financial transfers.
- real GDP | 实际国内生产总值 | Output valued at constant base-year prices | 用基年价格计算的 GDP，剔除了价格变化，衡量真实产量。 | Real GDP rose 2% even though nominal GDP rose 5%, because prices rose 3%. | 2 | #02-002
  vs: nominal GDP
- nominal GDP | 名义国内生产总值 | Output valued at current prices | 用当年价格计算的 GDP，会受到物价变动影响。 | Nominal GDP can rise purely because of inflation. | 2 | #02-003
  vs: real GDP
- GDP deflator | GDP 平减指数 | (Nominal GDP ÷ Real GDP) × 100, a price index for all final goods | 衡量所有最终产品价格水平的指数。 | If the GDP deflator is 110, prices are 10% higher than in the base year. | 3
- inflation | 通货膨胀 | A sustained rise in the general price level | 一般物价水平持续上升，货币购买力下降。 | Unexpected inflation hurts lenders who receive fixed interest payments. | 1 | #02-004
  rel: consumer price index; demand-pull inflation
- consumer price index | 消费者价格指数 | A price index for a fixed basket of goods bought by a typical consumer | 衡量典型消费者购买的一篮子商品价格变化的指数。 | The CPI may overstate inflation because of substitution bias. | 2 | #02-005
- unemployment rate | 失业率 | The number of unemployed divided by the labor force, times 100 | 失业人数占劳动力的百分比。灰心工人（discouraged workers）不计入劳动力。 | Discouraged workers leaving the labor force can lower the unemployment rate. | 2 | #02-006
- labor force participation rate | 劳动参与率 | The labor force as a percentage of the working-age civilian noninstitutional population | 劳动力占适龄平民人口的比例。 | Retirements of older workers reduce the labor force participation rate. | 2 | #02-007
- frictional unemployment | 摩擦性失业 | Unemployment from workers searching or transitioning between jobs | 工人在找工作或换工作期间的短期失业。 | A graduate searching for a first job is frictionally unemployed. | 2
  vs: structural unemployment
- structural unemployment | 结构性失业 | Unemployment from a mismatch between workers' skills and available jobs | 劳动者技能与岗位需求不匹配造成的失业，例如技术变革淘汰的岗位。 | Automation that replaces factory jobs causes structural unemployment. | 2
  vs: cyclical unemployment
- cyclical unemployment | 周期性失业 | Unemployment caused by a recession or decline in aggregate demand | 经济衰退、总需求下降造成的失业。 | Layoffs during a recession are cyclical unemployment. | 2
- natural rate of unemployment | 自然失业率 | The unemployment rate when cyclical unemployment is zero (frictional + structural) | 周期性失业为零时的失业率，对应充分就业。 | At full employment, the economy is at the natural rate of unemployment. | 3
- business cycle | 经济周期 | Short-run fluctuations in real GDP around its long-run trend | 实际 GDP 围绕长期趋势的波动：扩张、高峰、衰退、低谷。 | A recession is the contraction phase of the business cycle. | 1

@unit 3 | National Income and Price Determination | 国民收入与价格决定
- aggregate demand | 总需求 | Total planned spending on final goods and services at each price level: C + I + G + Xn | 各价格水平下对最终商品和服务的总计划支出。 | A rise in consumer confidence shifts aggregate demand right. | 2 | #02-008
  vis: supply-demand ad-as
- short-run aggregate supply | 短期总供给 | The output firms supply at each price level when some input prices are sticky | 部分投入价格黏性时，各价格水平下的总产出。 | A rise in oil prices shifts SRAS left, causing stagflation. | 2 | #02-009
  vs: long-run aggregate supply
- long-run aggregate supply | 长期总供给 | Potential output at full employment, vertical at the natural level of output | 充分就业时的潜在产出，是一条竖直线，与价格水平无关。 | LRAS is vertical because in the long run output depends on resources and technology, not prices. | 3 | #02-010
  vs: short-run aggregate supply
- multiplier | 乘数 | The ratio of the total change in GDP to an initial change in spending, 1/(1 − MPC) | 初始支出变化引起的 GDP 总变化倍数。MPC 越大，乘数越大。 | With MPC = 0.8, a $10 billion rise in spending increases GDP by up to $50 billion. | 3
  rel: marginal propensity to consume
- marginal propensity to consume | 边际消费倾向 | The fraction of additional income spent on consumption | 新增收入中用于消费的比例，MPC + MPS = 1。 | If MPC is 0.75, households spend 75 cents of each extra dollar. | 2
- recessionary gap | 衰退缺口 | When real output is below full-employment output | 实际产出低于充分就业产出，失业率高于自然失业率。 | Expansionary fiscal policy can close a recessionary gap. | 2
  vs: inflationary gap
- inflationary gap | 通胀缺口 | When real output is above full-employment output | 实际产出高于充分就业产出，物价上涨压力大。 | Contractionary policy can close an inflationary gap. | 2
  vs: recessionary gap
- stagflation | 滞胀 | Simultaneous inflation and high unemployment, often from a negative supply shock | 通货膨胀与高失业同时出现，通常由负面供给冲击引起。 | The 1970s oil shocks caused stagflation. | 3

@unit 4 | Financial Sector | 金融部门
- money supply | 货币供给 | The total quantity of money in an economy | 经济中货币的总量，由中央银行和银行体系决定。 | When the central bank buys bonds, the money supply increases. | 2
- money multiplier | 货币乘数 | 1 ÷ reserve requirement; the maximum expansion of deposits from new reserves | 新增准备金可创造的最大存款倍数。 | With a 10% reserve requirement, the money multiplier is 10. | 3 | #02-013
- reserve requirement | 法定准备金要求 | The fraction of deposits banks must hold as reserves | 银行必须保留的存款比例。 | Lowering the reserve requirement lets banks lend more. | 2 | #02-014
- open-market operations | 公开市场操作 | Central bank purchases or sales of government securities | 中央银行买卖政府债券来调节货币供给；买入债券增加货币供给。 | Buying bonds through open-market operations lowers interest rates. | 2 | #02-015
- nominal interest rate | 名义利率 | The interest rate not adjusted for inflation | 未扣除通货膨胀的利率。实际利率 ≈ 名义利率 − 通胀率。 | If the nominal rate is 6% and inflation is 2%, the real rate is about 4%. | 2
  vs: real interest rate
- real interest rate | 实际利率 | The interest rate adjusted for inflation | 扣除通货膨胀后的利率，影响投资决策。 | A higher real interest rate reduces investment spending. | 2
  vs: nominal interest rate
- loanable funds market | 可贷资金市场 | The market where savers supply funds and borrowers demand them, determining the real interest rate | 储蓄者提供资金、借款者需求资金并决定实际利率的市场。 | Government borrowing increases demand in the loanable funds market. | 3

@unit 5 | Long-Run Consequences of Stabilization Policies | 稳定政策的长期影响
- fiscal policy | 财政政策 | Government changes in spending and taxes to influence the economy | 政府通过改变支出和税收影响经济。扩张性：增支或减税。 | Cutting taxes during a recession is expansionary fiscal policy. | 2 | #02-011
  vs: monetary policy
- monetary policy | 货币政策 | Central bank actions that change the money supply and interest rates | 中央银行通过调整货币供给和利率影响经济。 | Lowering the policy rate is expansionary monetary policy. | 2 | #02-012
  vs: fiscal policy
- crowding out | 挤出效应 | Reduced private investment caused by government borrowing that raises interest rates | 政府借款推高利率，导致私人投资减少。 | Deficit spending may crowd out private investment. | 3 | #02-016
- Phillips curve | 菲利普斯曲线 | The short-run inverse relationship between inflation and unemployment | 短期内通货膨胀率与失业率之间的反向关系；长期菲利普斯曲线是竖直的。 | Moving up the short-run Phillips curve, lower unemployment comes with higher inflation. | 3 | #02-017
- budget deficit | 财政赤字 | When government spending exceeds tax revenue in a year | 一年内政府支出超过税收收入。 | A budget deficit adds to the national debt. | 2
  vs: national debt
- national debt | 国债（国家债务） | The total accumulated government borrowing | 政府历年借款的累积总额。 | Years of deficits increase the national debt. | 2
  vs: budget deficit

@unit 6 | Open Economy: International Trade and Finance | 开放经济：国际贸易与金融
- balance of payments | 国际收支 | The record of all transactions between a country and the rest of the world | 一国与世界其他国家所有交易的记录，包括经常账户和金融账户。 | A current account deficit is balanced by a financial account surplus. | 3
- current account | 经常账户 | The part of the balance of payments recording trade in goods and services, income and transfers | 记录商品服务贸易、收入和转移支付的账户。 | Importing more than exporting creates a current account deficit. | 3
- foreign exchange market | 外汇市场 | The market where currencies are traded | 各国货币兑换的市场，汇率由供需决定。 | Higher US interest rates increase demand for dollars in the foreign exchange market. | 2 | #02-018
- appreciation | 升值 | An increase in a currency's value relative to another currency | 一国货币相对其他货币价值上升，使出口更贵、进口更便宜。 | When the dollar appreciates, US exports become more expensive abroad. | 2 | #02-019
  vs: depreciation
- depreciation | 贬值 | A decrease in a currency's value relative to another currency | 一国货币相对其他货币价值下降，使出口更便宜。 | A depreciation of the yen makes Japanese cars cheaper for Americans. | 2 | #02-020
  vs: appreciation

@q macro-u2-001 | UNDERSTAND | CONCEPT | SCENARIO | 2 | 2 | structural unemployment; cyclical unemployment
? A coal miner loses her job because power plants switch to natural gas, and she lacks the skills for available jobs. This is
= cyclical unemployment. :: Her job loss is not caused by a recession.
=* structural unemployment. :: Correct — a lasting change in the economy created a skills mismatch.
= frictional unemployment. :: Frictional unemployment is short-term job searching.
= seasonal unemployment. :: The change is permanent, not seasonal.
! Structural unemployment results from mismatches between workers' skills and jobs, often after technological or industry change.
!zh 结构性失业源于技能与岗位不匹配，常由技术或产业变化引起。
@q macro-u3-001 | APPLY | APPLICATION | MCQ | 3 | 3 | multiplier; marginal propensity to consume
? If the MPC is 0.9, what is the maximum change in real GDP from a $20 billion increase in government spending?
= $18 billion :: That multiplies by the MPC, not the multiplier.
= $22 billion :: The multiplier is 10, not 1.1.
=* $200 billion :: Correct — multiplier = 1/(1 − 0.9) = 10.
= $2 billion :: That divides instead of multiplying.
! Spending multiplier = 1/(1 − MPC) = 1/0.1 = 10; 10 × $20 billion = $200 billion.
!zh 支出乘数 = 1/(1 − MPC) = 10，10 × 200 亿 = 2000 亿美元。
@q macro-u4-001 | APPLY | APPLICATION | SCENARIO | 4 | 2 | open-market operations; monetary policy
? To fight a recession, the central bank should
=* buy government bonds on the open market. :: Correct — buying bonds increases reserves and the money supply.
= sell government bonds on the open market. :: Selling bonds reduces the money supply.
= raise the reserve requirement. :: That reduces lending.
= raise taxes. :: Taxes are fiscal policy, not monetary policy.
! Expansionary monetary policy: buy bonds, lower the reserve requirement or lower the discount/policy rate.
!zh 扩张性货币政策：买入债券、降低准备金率或降低贴现率/政策利率。

@pair fiscal-vs-monetary | fiscal policy | monetary policy
! Fiscal policy uses government spending and taxes (decided by the legislature); monetary policy uses the money supply and interest rates (decided by the central bank).
!zh 财政政策：政府支出与税收（立法机构决定）；货币政策：货币供给与利率（中央银行决定）。
d: Tools :: Spending, taxes :: Open-market operations, reserve requirement, policy rates
d: Who decides :: Government / legislature :: Central bank
s: A :: Congress passes a tax cut to boost spending. :: Taxes = fiscal.
s: B :: The Federal Reserve buys Treasury bonds. :: Open-market operation = monetary.
s: B :: The central bank lowers the interest rate on reserves. :: Interest-rate tool = monetary.
s: A :: The government funds a new highway program. :: Spending = fiscal.
@pair real-vs-nominal-gdp | real GDP | nominal GDP
! Nominal GDP uses current prices; real GDP uses constant base-year prices, so only real GDP measures changes in actual output.
!zh 名义 GDP 用当年价格；实际 GDP 用基年不变价格，只有实际 GDP 能衡量真实产量变化。
s: B :: GDP rose 6% this year, but half of that was price increases. :: Unadjusted for prices.
s: A :: Output measured in 2017 dollars rose 3%. :: Constant prices.
s: A :: Used to compare living standards over decades. :: Removes inflation effects.
s: B :: Calculated using this year's prices. :: Current prices.
